  "properties": {
    "title": "Pacific EEZ polygons",
    "description": "200 NM Exclusive Economic Zones of the 22 Pacific Island countries and territories, plus flagged overlapping claims and joint regimes (nests = false). Boundaries are not legally authoritative. Sources: Flanders Marine Institute (VLIZ), Marine Regions, \"Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Maritime Boundaries and Exclusive Economic Zones (200NM), version 12\" (marineregions-eez-v12); Pacific Community (SPC), Geoscience, Energy and Maritime Division, \"Global Exclusive Economic Zones (200 Nautical Miles) - Merged Dataset (SPC Pacific Maritime Boundaries)\" (spc-gem-pacific-eez-200nm). Licences (per row in the `license` column): CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0, CC-BY-4.0. Some rows are used and redistributed by this project under a data-use agreement (CSDR-SPC data use agreement (user-confirmed 2026-11-20)); downstream users are bound by the row's public licence (e.g. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) unless they hold their own agreement. Full provenance and source notes: https://github.com/SustainableDevelopmentReform/pacific-administrative-boundaries/blob/v0.1.0/docs/sources.md#eez.",
